sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Morphometric validation: 55/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "Quantitative metrics are computed on the output and compared with literature values: the map's magnification against Horton & Hoyt's human M(E) = 17.3/(E + 0.75) over 1-40 deg (RMS 6.8%, A = 18.72 vs 17.3, E2 = 1.71 vs 0.75 deg, extent 74.6 vs 83.0 mm), and the rendered cycle count and lambda_c against the paper's 30-36 stripes and 2.4-3.2 mm. Deductions: the headline comparison fails - lambda_c is 3.1x too long and 11 cycles vs 30-36 stripes - and the failure is disclosed but not resolved or explained by a parameter choice traced to the paper (-12); the FFT k* and azimuthal class validate the rendering against its own q*-derived cycle count, which is circular (-8); no morphometric of the retinal pullbacks (ring count per degree, spiral pitch angle, arm count, cobweb spoke count) is compared with Klüver's reports or Bressloff Fig. 1 (-10); the Rule (2011) RMS beta error 0.154 is a fixture-internal comparison to digitised model curves whose source file is not vendored, not a comparison to flicker-phosphene psychophysics (-5); the Horton & Hoyt self-test threshold of 25% RMS is lenient given a 30% maximum relative error at 1 deg and E2 more than twice the empirical value (-5); the Gaussian-only negative control is a correct and credited sanity check. Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L185–L216: compare_cortical_magnification: RMS and max relative error vs Horton & Hoyt over 1-40 deg; the one comparison to measured human data <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L185-L216>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L219–L256: compare_paper_scale_anchors: lambda_c 8.68 mm vs 2.4-3.2 mm (ratio 3.1), 11 cycles vs 30-36 stripes, disclosed not corrected <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L219-L256>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L2576–L2593: Self-test checks k* equals the rendered cycle count derived from the same q* - a self-consistency check, not a specimen comparison <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L2576-L2593>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L2487–L2493: Horton & Hoyt acceptance threshold 25% RMS; max_abs_rel_error 0.30 and E2 1.71 vs 0.75 deg pass under it <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L2487-L2493>. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): bressloff-v1-form-constants stability_reports parity, max |Δ| = 0.0 dimensionless (reference 0.0, MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants commit 344863a1bd9e8a8e8c9cb20aced2897f3ffb2c4c) [maximum absolute error across all 5 Bressloff (2001) stability_reports (q*, λ*, γ(0), γ(θ), η_hex) vs paper-calibration.json]; Mexican-hat lateral inhibition critical wavenumber q* (Bressloff 2001 Fig. 16) = 1.028 dimensionless wavenumber (reference >0.5 (finite Turing/Euclidean symmetry-breaking wavelength), Bressloff et al. 2001 Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 356:299 Fig. 16) [maximizer of max(λ_even(q), λ_odd(q)) with lateral_inhibition = 0.27] — interior peak prominence = 0.1200; Gaussian-only negative control critical wavenumber q* (lateral_inhibition = 0) = 0.05 dimensionless wavenumber (reference 0.05, q_min boundary of [0.05, 3.0] grid (monotonically decaying dispersion, prominence = 0.0)) [maximizer of λ(q) when Mexican-hat surround inhibition is removed (lateral_inhibition = 0.0)] — interior peak prominence = 0.00e+00; Klüver Tunnel/Rings cortical planform spectral ring sharpness = 31.331 ratio (peak/median PSD) (reference >5.0, Bressloff et al. 2001 Fig. 7 / Klüver 1966 Tunnel form constant) [2D FFT radial power spectrum peak/median ratio at k* = 11 cycles]; Klüver Honeycomb/Hex linear cortical planform spectral ring wavenumber k* = 11.0 cycles / domain (reference 11 (q*/d_hyp = 11.27 cycles), Bressloff et al. 2001 Fig. 35 / Klüver 1966 Honeycomb form constant) [dominant radial FFT wavenumber of the linear 3-mode hexagonal eigenmode superposition (non-contoured, weak tanh); the rendered wavenumber is q*/d_hyp quantised to integer cycles on the 2πβ/ε torus] — contoured-rendering k* = 21 = 2k harmonic of tanh∘max (normalised power at k/√3k/2k = 0.50/0.68/1.00); FFT lattice class = hexagonal; Retino-cortical magnification vs Horton & Hoyt (1991), RMS relative error over 1-40 deg = 0.0678 dimensionless (reference 0 (perfect agreement); map-implied A = α/ε = 18.72 mm/deg, E2 = w0/ε = 1.71 deg vs 17.3, 0.75, Horton & Hoyt 1991 Arch. Ophthalmol. 109:816 (doi:10.1001/archopht.1991.01080060080030); datasets/bressloff/horton_hoyt_1991_magnification.json) [RMS of (α/(w0+εr) − 17.3/(E+0.75)) / (17.3/(E+0.75)) over 157 eccentricities in [1, 40] deg] — max |rel err| = 0.300; fovea→90° extent 74.6 mm (model) vs 83.0 mm (H&H); Upstream fixture paper-expectation checks passed (paper-calibration.json, stability_reports + runs) = 121.0 count (reference 133.0, MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants commit 344863a1bd9e8a8e8c9cb20aced2897f3ffb2c4c, stability_reports[*].checks and runs[*].checks) [number of the fixture's own expected-vs-actual checks that pass, out of 133 (stability_reports 10/11, runs 111/122; run status {'pass': 17, 'review': 7})] — fig40_odd_hex_bifurcation/selected-pattern: expected triangle, actual honeycomb; fig31_square_even/same-lattice-branch-pattern: expected cobweb, actual spiral; fig31_square_even/same-lattice-branch-family: expected square, actual roll; fig32_square_odd/same-lattice-branch-pattern: expected cobweb, actual spiral; fig32_square_odd/same-lattice-branch-family: expected square, actual roll; fig35_hex_even/same-lattice-branch-pattern: expected hex_pi, actual honeycomb; fig36_triangle_odd/same-lattice-branch-pattern: expected triangle, actual honeycomb; fig5_hex_cortical/same-lattice-branch-pattern: expected hex_pi, actual honeycomb; fig5_square_cortical/same-lattice-branch-pattern: expected cobweb, actual spiral; fig5_square_cortical/same-lattice-branch-family: expected square, actual roll; fig6_visual_field_planforms/same-lattice-branch-pattern: expected cobweb, actual spiral; fig6_visual_field_planforms/same-lattice-branch-family: expected square, actual roll; Preset runs reproduced with exact parity (paper-calibration.json runs[]) = 24.0 count (reference 24.0, MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants commit 344863a1bd9e8a8e8c9cb20aced2897f3ffb2c4c, runs[*]) [runs whose critical_q, critical_branch, selected family/pattern/scope and rendered pattern match the fixture, out of 24] — max |Δq*| = 2.22e-16; Gallery panels whose rendered lattice is the branch the cubic amplitude equations select (rhombic angle free) = 1.0 count (reference 5.0, Bressloff et al. 2001 §5 cubic amplitude equations (Eqs. 5.9-5.15), evaluated by branch_selection_for()) [rendered family == unrestricted_selected_family, out of 5 gallery panels; 1 further panels are linearly stable branches that lose the Lyapunov tie-break, 3 are imposed (unstable at cubic order)] — fig7_lattice_tunnel: imposed-unstable; fig33_rhombic_even_roll: imposed-unstable; fig31_square_even: imposed-unstable; fig35_hex_zero_even: stable-coexisting; fig33_rhombic_even: selected; Rendered cortical wavelength λ_c relative to the paper's stated 2.4-3.2 mm = 3.1006 ratio (reference 1.0 (paper scale); paper also states 30-36 perceived stripes vs 11 rendered cycles, Bressloff et al. 2002 Neural Comput. 14:473 §1.1) [λ_c = 2π d_hyp / q* (d_hyp = 2 mm, q* from the gallery preset) divided by the midpoint 2.8 mm of Bressloff 2002 §1.1's 2.4-3.2 mm] — λ_c = 8.68 mm; foveal magnification 10.98 vs 11.5 mm/deg (α = 3/π from upstream params.rs vs α ≈ 1.00 implied by the paper); Spiral retinal pullback mirror symmetry (full-field convention) = -0.0291 Pearson r (reference 1.000 (bilateral-mirror mode, same preset), Bressloff et al. 2001 Fig. 33b / 2002 §1.1 (logarithmic spirals are oblique rolls under the complex-log map)) [correlation between the retinal field and its left-right reflection; chiral spirals give |r| << 1, the bilateral-mirror convention gives 1.0] — left-horizontal-meridian seam contrast 9.9x (full-field) vs 1.0x (mirror); Critical-branch parity flips over the lateral-spread sweep θ₀ ∈ [0°, 90°] = 2.0 count (reference ≥1 (Bressloff 2001 §4: even planforms selected for θ₀ ≳ 45°), Bressloff et al. 2001 Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 356:299 §4, Figs. 16-17) [number of even↔odd changes of the maximal-growth branch across 31 sweep points (fig17_even base)] — flips at θ₀ ≈ [45, 90]°; q* over ξ̂_lat 1.5→6: 1.46→0.70; Rule et al. (2011) Fig. 8 overlay domain-normalised RMS β error (diagnostic, no calibration claim) = 0.154 normalised wavenumber β (reference <= 0.10 acceptance threshold (NOT met), Rule, Stoffregen & Ermentrout 2011 PLoS Comput. Biol. 7:e1002158 Fig. 8 via upstream fixture) [rule-2011-floquet.json source_curve_comparison.domain_beta_mapping.rms_error] — acceptance_status = outside-threshold-diagnostic; calibration_claim_allowed = False." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-morphometric-validation> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.55"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-morphometric-validation> rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants (2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py, docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif, bressloff_v1_metrics.csv, datasets/bressloff/horton_hoyt_1991_magnification.json) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Morphometric validation' for Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes" ;
        dct:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (primary) + Gemini 4 Argon (independent blinded second assessor)" .
}

sub:provenance {
    sub:assertion prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1001/archopht.1991.01080060080030>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00336965>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.2000.0769>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1137/23M1616686>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1162/089976602317250861>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002158> .
    <https://doi.org/10.1001/archopht.1991.01080060080030> dct:date "1991"^^xsd:gYear ;
        dct:title "The representation of the visual field in human striate cortex: a revision of the classic Holmes map" .
    <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00336965> dct:date "1979"^^xsd:gYear ;
        dct:title "A mathematical theory of visual hallucination patterns" .
    <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.2000.0769> dct:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
        dct:title "Geometric visual hallucinations, Euclidean symmetry and the functional architecture of striate cortex" .
    <https://doi.org/10.1137/23M1616686> dct:date "2024"^^xsd:gYear ;
        dct:title "A mathematical model of the visual MacKay effect" .
    <https://doi.org/10.1162/089976602317250861> dct:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
        dct:title "What geometric visual hallucinations tell us about the visual cortex" .
    <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002158> dct:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
        dct:title "A model for the origin and properties of flicker-induced geometric phosphenes" .
}

